@ymodak 

I'd really like if you (and the Keras team) could look into this as soon as possible, so that I can start relevant development and training. 
There are 36 models to train (12 each of X, Y and Z) and each one takes roughly >20 hours. So it'd be great if we could start soon.

@fchollet you probably missed out but @AdityaKane2001 has actually trained the models he's talking about as a part of his GSoC 2021 project (I was one of his mentors). 

The entire collection is available [here](https://tfhub.dev/adityakane2001/collections/regnety/1) on TensorFlow Hub. However, he wants to work on a more streamlined version of RegNets (model building wise) and train those variants once again. He has Cloud TPU access and a reproducible training pipeline already developed (refer [here](https://github.com/AdityaKane2001/regnety)) for that. 

So, if you provide the green signal he could start working on it ASAP. I'll also be keen to take part in the reviews :)

@innat 

In my honest opinion, Regnets are celebrated for their efficiency and scalability. They beat ResNet and Efficientnet scores using lesser flops than them, especially at higher flop regimes. 

Honestly I also think you are referring to the wrong Regnets, as there are many papers with the same name, which are not as popular.

![IMG_20210918_205020.jpg](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/64411306/133893773-cf96d9d8-5cf6-4e03-b4ba-67556022c3de.jpg)

@sayakpaul 

Thanks for the clarification!

@AdityaKane2001 
Yes, my information source was wrong. Thanks to @sayakpaul.  

FYI, Please don't get too excited to see the claim to beat EfficientNet. In fact, they don't really respect the scaling and training process in the original EfficientNet paper during comparison; [link](https://github.com/facebookresearch/pycls/issues/116). Facebook claimed to beat EfficientNet with RegNet but people like Ross Wightman ([timm](https://twitter.com/wightmanr/status/1262516105240813568?lang=en)) found the opposite during retraining especially for larger input resolution.
